      "  6. Apply the decision table (CI fail / any 🔴/🟡 → REQUEST_CHANGES; else APPROVE).",
      "  7. Post a GitHub APPROVE or REQUEST_CHANGES review.",
      `  8. Write \`result.json\` to \`${resultPath}\` with:`,
      '     `{ "terminal_status": "passed" | "change_requested" | "escalate", ... }`',
      "",
      "Complete all steps without stopping or asking for confirmation.",
    ],
    modelSection(reviewerModel),
    [
      "## Rules",
      "",
      "- Do not ask clarifying questions.",
      "- Use `GITHUB_TOKEN` from the environment for all GitHub API calls.",
      "- Read documents in the specified order before evaluating the diff.",
      "- Every finding must cite the exact file path and line from the diff.",
      "- Every finding must cite the specific rubric criterion that was violated.",
      "- Do not request changes that contradict the approved product spec.",
      `- Always write \`${resultPath}\` as the final step — even on failure.`,
      "- If any shell command exits with code 127 (command not found), write",
      `  \`{"terminal_status":"escalate","verdict":"escalate","confidence":0,"notes":"missing_tool"}\``,
      `  to \`${resultPath}\` and stop immediately.`,
    ],
  );
}

